error[ffi_lock_copied]: this copies a `Box`, whose C struct `struct box` holds a `pthread_mutex_t` at `m`, which C forbids to copy
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-lock-copied-a-c-parameter-by-value-is-told-at-the-argument.hero:17:20
     |
  17 |     print(box_peek(m))  #~ ffi_lock_copied
     |                    ^
  note: a copy of a lock is a second lock holding the first one's state: the copy of a held mutex reads held, and unlocking one leaves the other locked
  note: lend the place instead: a function taking `c: T lent` reads the caller's own cell and changes nothing, `f(c)`; one taking `@c` may change it, `f(@c)`; a field is read in place, `c.n`
